Activated Sludge and Aerobic Biofilm Reactors — von Sperling (@wu-bw5: 0, is #reference, #part-of @wu-sources) { r_0WMGVEM60J63M01SJJDQ9357GE
Marcos von Sperling. Biological Wastewater Treatment Series, volume 5, IWA Publishing, 2007. [Persistent publisher reference](https://doi.org/10.2166/9781780402123).

Read the complete suspended-growth and attached-growth treatment argument. Work balances connecting liquid residence time, biomass age, substrate, oxygen, recycle, wasting and separation. Compare operating changes that have the same nominal flow but different biological consequences.

The title belongs to the publisher's open-access series. Consult this edition's actual rights and retain its notices. Continue with the later [Biological Wastewater Treatment — Chen and colleagues, second edition](Biological-Wastewater-Treatment-Chen-and-Colleagues.lingua#r_1AE9DK0YWQR5GDECZ9KK1JJP37) treatment for advanced nutrient removal, biofilms, modelling and control.

